          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which of the following systemic conditions is NOT associated with HLA-B27-related anterior uveitis?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ankylosing spondylitis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Ankylosing spondylitis is the most classic HLA-B27 spondyloarthropathy associated with acute anterior uveitis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rheumatoid arthritis</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Rheumatoid arthritis is not part of the HLA-B27 spondyloarthropathy group. The associated conditions are ankylosing spondylitis, reactive arthritis, psoriatic arthritis, and inflammatory bowel disease.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Reactive arthritis</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Reactive arthritis is a spondyloarthropathy within the HLA-B27 spectrum and is associated with anterior uveitis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Inflammatory bowel disease</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Inflammatory bowel disease (Crohn's disease and ulcerative colitis) is part of the HLA-B27 spondyloarthropathy group associated with anterior uveitis.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Rheumatoid arthritis is explicitly absent from the HLA-B27 spondyloarthropathy group. The four associated conditions are ankylosing spondylitis, reactive arthritis, psoriatic arthritis, and inflammatory bowel disease."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Despite being a common arthritis, rheumatoid arthritis does not belong to the HLA-B27 spondyloarthropathy group and is not a recognised cause of anterior uveitis."
                }
              ],
